  "answer": "I'll start by reading the project skills that apply to this cart-limit change, then look through the storefront cart API.The request already spells out the limit, the config key, and the 400 response, so I\u2019ll implement it directly and look up how the storefront cart and merchant settings work.The cart limit is a small, fully specified change. I\u2019ll add a failing test for the quantity rule, then enforce it on the storefront cart endpoints.The storefront cart API now rejects any create, add, or quantity change that would leave a line with more units than the store allows. The limit is the merchant configuration value `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY`, read on each request so a change applies without a restart, and it defaults to 99 when that setting is missing. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Requests over the limit return HTTP 400 and the cart is not changed.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am test -Dtest=CartMaxLineQuantityTest -DfailIfNoTests=false -q\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 from the live cart endpoints and that an existing cart is unchanged, because the integration suite was not run\"], \"missing\": [\"a documented integration test that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and posts to POST /api/v1/cart, PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}, and POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi\"]}",
